WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.650
- [Narrator] This Great Big
Story was made possible,

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.200
by the Singapore Tourism Board.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.710
- Hip-hop is the truest representation

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.530
of who you are and where you're from.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.800
I grew up experiencing
this beautiful duality

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.800
of Tamil and English.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.270
Tamil is one of the five

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.880
most commonly spoken Indian languages.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.870
Tamil is a huge part of who I am,

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.820
and when I chose to pursue music,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.513
I could not do it without
Tamil being in the picture.

00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:37.270
(funky music)

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.750
My name is Yung Raja.
I'm a Singaporean rapper.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.653
I rap in English and Tamil.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.840
My family moved from South India

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.710
to Singapore in 1992.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.450
Growing up, I spent most of
my time thinking in Tamil

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.020
and writing in Tamil.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:56.120
For me, it was an idea
mixing the Tamil that I know;

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.510
how do we put that and English
into the equation of hip-hop?

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.363
That was the question that
I was trying to solve.

00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:09.630
The first ever experiment we did,

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.930
was to make a remix of
Lil Pump's “Gucci Gang,”

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.310
and we called it “Poori Gang,”

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.250
and poori is a very famous Indian dish.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.093
That was very well received.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.520
The blend of Tamil and
English is just seamless;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.961
you don't feel like I'm mixing
another foreign language.

00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:30.794
♪ Mustafa by Yung Raja ♪

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.338
Something really interesting
has been happening recently,

00:01:38.338 --> 00:01:41.170
with the world of hip-hop.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:42.770
You see people like Rich Brian,

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.400
you see people like Higher Brothers

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.570
that pursue hip-hop and rap
with their mother tongue.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.080
There's something very unique about this

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.080
because Asian hip-hop, I
think, is so, so beautiful.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.371
You are adding another
language that carries

00:01:58.371 --> 00:02:01.450
so many stories, so much
history, so much heritage.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.350
So that's like, that changes the game.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.090
This is the greatest thing about hip-hop:

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.700
when you let people know where you're from

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.810
and what you stand for
and what you represent,

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.210
people respect you.

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.980
Peace, it's your boy, Yung Raja.

